WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.955
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:08.746
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:16.540
Unit two: Reading: Complete the Words. Today you will restore missing letters in a short passage using context and spelling.

4
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.504
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.537
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.431
Context.

7
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.450
Context means the words around a word that give meaning.

8
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.108
Use context to find the word.

9
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:35.218
Your turn. Say: Context.

10
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.103
Context.

11
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:40.874
Prefix.

12
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.591
Prefix means letters added to the start of a word.

13
00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:46.672
Un is a prefix.

14
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.901
Your turn. Say: Prefix.

15
00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:53.779
Prefix.

16
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:55.611
Suffix.

17
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:59.545
Suffix means letters added to the end of a word.

18
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.662
Ing is a suffix.

19
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.891
Your turn. Say: Suffix.

20
00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:08.781
Suffix.

21
00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:10.297
Missing.

22
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:12.772
Missing means not there.

23
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:15.104
The missing letters are at the end.

24
00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:17.510
Your turn. Say: Missing.

25
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.391
Missing.

26
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.047
Spelling.

27
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.421
Spelling means the correct letters in a word.

28
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:28.320
Check each spelling.

29
00:01:28.917 --> 00:01:31.151
Your turn. Say: Spelling.

30
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.048
Spelling.

31
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:36.959
Part of speech.

32
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.994
Part of speech means a word class such as noun or verb.

33
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.200
Decide the part of speech.

34
00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:46.958
Your turn. Say: Part of speech.

35
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.033
Part of speech.

36
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:52.773
Logical.

37
00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:55.841
Logical means making sense.

38
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.090
Choose the logical word.

39
00:01:58.683 --> 00:02:01.173
Your turn. Say: Logical.

40
00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.104
Logical.

41
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:06.758
Skim.

42
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.667
Skim means to read quickly for the general idea.

43
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:12.842
Skim the passage first.

44
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.835
Your turn. Say: Skim.

45
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.631
Skim.

46
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:24.316
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.568
Visal, what do you do in Complete the Words?

48
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:39.439
You read a short academic paragraph where some words have missing letters. You type the missing letters so that every word is correct and the passage makes sense.

49
00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.166
What is the best first step?

50
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:54.354
Skim the whole paragraph to understand the topic. Then look at each incomplete word and use the sentence, the part of speech and the letters you already have.

51
00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.055
What mistakes should I avoid?

52
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:10.590
Do not guess random letters. Check the spelling, and remember prefixes and suffixes such as un-, re-, -ing and -tion, which often appear at the beginning or end.

53
00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.222
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:18.533
Grammar focus: Strategy: context, part of speech, spelling.

55
00:03:18.833 --> 00:03:20.054
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.212
The word needs a verb, so I look for -ed, -ing or -s.

57
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:28.788
The sentence is about plants, so the missing word is probably growth.

58
00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:36.786
Read the whole paragraph first, then use the topic, the grammar and the visible letters to complete each word. Always check spelling.

59
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.003
Be careful! Don't say: I guess random letters.

60
00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:45.825
Say: I use context and spelling.

61
00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.660
Use context clues.

62
00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:51.374
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.609
A Short Paragraph.

64
00:03:53.909 --> 00:03:57.220
The paragraph is about how plants grow in dry areas.

65
00:03:58.233 --> 00:04:00.581
Some words have only the first half written.

66
00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.797
Ravy decides that the first missing word must be a noun.

67
00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.937
She uses the letters she can see to choose the right word.

68
00:04:09.933 --> 00:04:12.583
She checks the spelling of each completed word.

69
00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:17.796
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.684
Complete the Words is a blank task.

71
00:04:20.984 --> 00:04:24.162
A, Speaking. B, Listening. C, Reading.

72
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.746
The answer is C: Reading.

73
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:32.210
First you should blank.

74
00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:37.069
A, skim the paragraph. B, type quickly. C, skip it.

75
00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:43.039
The answer is A: skim the paragraph.

76
00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.334
Prefixes and suffixes are blank.

77
00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:50.554
A, numbers. B, word parts. C, maps.

78
00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.459
The answer is B: word parts.

79
00:04:57.617 --> 00:04:59.361
What is the paragraph about?

80
00:04:59.661 --> 00:05:04.638
A, a city map. B, a phone call. C, plants in dry areas.

81
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.908
The answer is C: plants in dry areas.

82
00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.748
What does Ravy check last?

83
00:05:14.048 --> 00:05:17.724
A, spelling. B, the title. C, the time zone.

84
00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.092
The answer is A: spelling.

85
00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.544
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:28.383 --> 00:05:30.627
How do you complete missing letters in a word?

87
00:05:39.417 --> 00:05:40.952
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:41.252 --> 00:05:52.974
I read the whole paragraph to understand the topic. Then I decide the part of speech and use the letters I can see to find the word. At the end I check the spelling of every word.

89
00:05:53.274 --> 00:05:55.100
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:55.983 --> 00:06:01.968
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: context, part of speech, spelling.

91
00:06:02.268 --> 00:06:07.660
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.299
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

93
00:06:10.599 --> 00:06:13.716
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

